            "situation": "This patient has been referred on the two-week-wait (2WW) pathway for suspected cancer. The summary is being produced for clinician review to assess the referral and determine the most appropriate action under the Faster Diagnosis pathway. **No demographic information (age, sex, date of birth) is available in the source data.**",
            "background": "- Suspected upper gastrointestinal cancer (referred on 2WW pathway)\n- Progressive dysphagia over 10 weeks, initially solids only, now affecting semi-solids [2026-05-04]\n- Unintentional weight loss of 6 kilograms over 2 months [2026-05-04]\n- Persistent upper abdominal pain in epigastric region (5/10, not relieved by antacids) [2026-05-04]\n- Recent vomiting (two episodes in past fortnight, occurring hours after eating) [2026-05-04]\n- Blood results [2026-04-28]: Hb 144.5 g/L (normal), platelets slightly raised at 465 x10^9/L, ALT mildly elevated at 68.8 U/L, alkaline phosphatase raised at 155 U/L, ferritin elevated at 384.8 ug/L",
            "assessment": "**2 guideline rule(s) fired** (scope: guidelines NG12).\n\n### Routine\n- **Rule: 1.2.1** _(strength: refer)_ -- rule `rule:NG12:v1:CH002:SEC001:R000:7b7e6325`\n  - Recommendation: 1.2.1 Refer people using a suspected cancer pathway referral for oesophageal cancer if they: have dysphagia or are aged 55\u00a0and over, with weight loss, and they have any of the following: upper abdominal pain reflux dyspepsia. [2015, amended 2025]\n  - Matched on: Difficulty swallowing; Unintentional weight loss; Upper abdominal pain\n  - Action: Fast track referral for suspected upper gastrointestinal cancer (procedure)\n  - Guideline: Suspected cancer: recognition and referral (`NG12`)\n- **Rule: 1.2.7** _(strength: refer)_ -- rule `rule:NG12:v1:CH002:SEC001:R006:da4bdbcb:edit:e12353e8`\n  - Recommendation: 1.2.7 Refer people using a suspected cancer pathway referral for stomach cancer if they: have dysphagia or are aged 55\u00a0and over, with weight loss, and they have any of the following: upper abdominal pain reflux dyspepsia. [2015, amended 2025]\n  - Matched on: Difficulty swallowing; a related coded finding for Weight decreased; Upper abdominal pain\n  - Action: Fast track referral for suspected upper gastrointestinal cancer (procedure)\n  - Guideline: Suspected cancer: recognition and referral (`NG12`)",
            "recommendation": "This patient meets the criteria for suspected upper gastrointestinal cancer referral on the two-week-wait pathway under NICE guideline NG12 [RULE: rule:NG12:v1:CH002:SEC001:R000:7b7e6325, RULE: rule:NG12:v1:CH002:SEC001:R006:da4bdbcb:edit:e12353e8]. The combination of progressive dysphagia, unintentional weight loss, and persistent upper abdominal pain triggers referral criteria for both oesophageal cancer (rule 1.2.1) and stomach cancer (rule 1.2.7). An urgent upper gastrointestinal endoscopy should be arranged within 14 days to investigate the cause of these symptoms and exclude malignancy. The patient should be safety-netted to return immediately if they develop new alarm symptoms such as haematemesis, melaena, or worsening dysphagia affecting liquids.",
